{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Introduce a 50% levy on new fossil fuel revenue for health & social care fund",
        "additional_details": "The levy should ensure that half of all future UK oil and gas revenues are put into a protected investment fund that will then grow over time. The revenue from the fund, not the savings, should go towards funding high-quality, affordable social and health care for everyone who needs it.\r\n \r\nThis could mean better care for older people and those with disabilities and better funded health care for all, a system that\u2019s fair, sustainable, and in place for future generations, and which ensures investment in the people of our country, rather than just spending whilst in the moment.",
        "background": "Introduce a levy on revenue from future fossil fuel exports to establish a UK social care investment fund (UKSCIF), modelled on the principles of sovereign wealth funds, which directly provides stable, long term funding support for health and social care across the UK.",
